    {
      "id": "confession",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 440,
        "y": 350
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "beat",
        "title": "I only held the rope",
        "description": "## Direction\n\nHobb is talking, or starting to. He begins where it hurts, with the rope, slowly and in pieces, wiping his face with his good hand, and he won't say more where the whole Rat can hear: the player has to find him somewhere quieter or give him a reason. The rest (his master, the Heron and tonight's loading, his token: see his secrets) comes out as the player asks for it, with no dice, one thing per reply and in his own words. He knows only his own part of the night, so he doesn't brief anyone on the Heron. Answer what they actually ask, and never put questions in their mouth or run the interview for them. If he thinks he's talking to his master's people (a trick that worked), he tells it as proof he has kept faith, and it's the same truth. Kell writes it all down. When it's out, he asks what's to become of him: he's terrified of the noose and more terrified of his master, and he has to be at the river door at the eleventh bell or his master will know something is wrong. The beat ends on the player's choice: Kell takes him in, he goes to work (as their man inside, or keeping his head down), or he runs. Don't decide it for them.\n\n## Cast in this beat\n\n### Big Hobb Mallory (hobb)\n\nTell the loft first, then answer what you're asked, one thing at a time: asked straight for the Master's name, you give it, in a whisper. When it's out, ask what's to become of you. The token's only brass: give it up if asked.\n\n### Sergeant Agnes Kell (kell)\n\nWrite it down. You have enough to take him in now, and you'll say so, once; whether you do it tonight is the investigator's call. If you do, it's by the book, outside Nan's door.\n\n### Nan Quill (nan-quill)\n\nKeep the room off his back, and keep your ears open.\n\n### Dilly Sparrow (dilly)\n\nSit with him. Glare at anyone who frightened it out of him.\n\n### Cob (cob)\n\nIf you're near enough to hear, listen from behind something.\n\n## Pressure\n\nThe eleventh bell rings across the water. Hobb gets to his feet, because he has to be at the river door when it stops.",
        "lore": [
          "Places/The Drowned Rat.md",
          "World/Caerwyn now.md",
          "World/Fronts.md",
          "Cast/Big Hobb Mallory/public.md",
          "Cast/Sergeant Agnes Kell/public.md",
          "Cast/Nan Quill/public.md",
          "Cast/Dilly Sparrow/public.md",
          "Cast/Cob/public.md"
        ],
        "sourceId": "confession",
        "sourceFile": "scenes/drowned-rat.ts",
        "sourceBeat": {
          "id": "confession",
          "title": "I only held the rope",
          "direction": "Hobb is talking, or starting to. He begins where it hurts, with the rope, slowly and in pieces, wiping his face with his good hand, and he won't say more where the whole Rat can hear: the player has to find him somewhere quieter or give him a reason. The rest (his master, the Heron and tonight's loading, his token: see his secrets) comes out as the player asks for it, with no dice, one thing per reply and in his own words. He knows only his own part of the night, so he doesn't brief anyone on the Heron. Answer what they actually ask, and never put questions in their mouth or run the interview for them. If he thinks he's talking to his master's people (a trick that worked), he tells it as proof he has kept faith, and it's the same truth. Kell writes it all down. When it's out, he asks what's to become of him: he's terrified of the noose and more terrified of his master, and he has to be at the river door at the eleventh bell or his master will know something is wrong. The beat ends on the player's choice: Kell takes him in, he goes to work (as their man inside, or keeping his head down), or he runs. Don't decide it for them.",
          "cast": {
            "hobb": "Tell the loft first, then answer what you're asked, one thing at a time: asked straight for the Master's name, you give it, in a whisper. When it's out, ask what's to become of you. The token's only brass: give it up if asked.",
            "kell": "Write it down. You have enough to take him in now, and you'll say so, once; whether you do it tonight is the investigator's call. If you do, it's by the book, outside Nan's door.",
            "nan-quill": "Keep the room off his back, and keep your ears open.",
            "dilly": "Sit with him. Glare at anyone who frightened it out of him.",
            "cob": "If you're near enough to hear, listen from behind something."
          },
          "pressure": "The eleventh bell rings across the water. Hobb gets to his feet, because he has to be at the river door when it stops.",
          "transitions": [
            {
              "id": "told-heron",
              "when": "The player asks Hobb where he works, or where he's due at the bell, what goes on there tonight or how a body gets in, or Hobb tells it. No dice: the loft is out, and the rest comes as he's asked. He tells his own part of the night as he knows it: the Heron warehouse, at the downriver end of the wharves, re-sacking ('It's the King's grain, sir. Everyone knows. Nobody says.'); tonight's a loading night, with a barge for Saltmere; he's due on the hoist at the eleventh bell, the gang go in at the river door off the plank walk, showing a brass heron token at its grille, and the Master comes at the midnight bell to see the barge off.",
              "to": "confession",
              "establishes": [
                "The player knows that Hobb does night work at the Heron warehouse, at the downriver end of the wharves."
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "told-master",
              "when": "The player asks Hobb straight for his master's name (who he is, who he does it for, who 'the Master' is), or Hobb gives it. No dice: the loft is out, and the rest comes as he's asked. It costs him most, so it comes in a whisper, with a look at the door: Master Sallow of the Royal Purveyor's office, who struck the clerk with the head of his cane and used the cord.",
              "to": "confession",
              "establishes": [
                "Big Hobb has named his master to the player: Master Sallow of the Royal Purveyor's office."
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "token-given",
              "when": "The player asks Hobb for his brass river-door token (the heron on the greasy string round his neck), or Hobb hands it over, to the player or to Kell. No dice: it's only brass, and the gang know his face at the grille, so he has no need of it tonight. He pulls it over his head and holds it out: shown at the grille of the Heron's river door, it gets the bolt drawn.",
              "to": "confession",
              "establishes": [
                "Hobb has handed over his brass river-door token for the Heron warehouse."
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "inside-man",
              "when": "The player asks Hobb to be their man inside the Heron tonight (to open the river door to their knock, keep the gang off them, or point out the clerk's book) once his mum is to be kept safe tonight or they've made him a promise that truly answers his fear, or Hobb has agreed to it. No dice: he swallows, nods and says he'll do it, for as long as his nerve holds.",
              "to": "confession",
              "establishes": [
                "Hobb has agreed to be the player's man inside the Heron tonight."
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "turn-hobb",
              "on": "attempt",
              "when": "The player tries to talk Hobb into going back into the Heron tonight as their man inside, while his fear of his master could still win: his mum isn't safe yet, and nothing they've promised answers his fear. (Once his mum is to be kept safe tonight, or for a promise that truly answers his fear, it needs no dice: that isn't this.)",
              "check": {
                "reason": "to talk Hobb into being your man inside the Heron",
                "skill": "persuasion",
                "dc": 14,
                "success": "Hobb swallows, nods and says he'll do it: he'll open the river door to their knock and keep the gang off them, for as long as his nerve holds.",
                "failure": "He can't. He'll go to work, because not going would tell his master everything, but in there he'll keep his head down and pray; he won't lift a finger for them.",
                "onSuccess": "confession",
                "establishes": {
                  "success": [
                    "Hobb has agreed to be the player's man inside the Heron tonight."
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "let-him-go",
              "on": "attempt",
              "when": "The player is done at the Rat: they leave with what Hobb told them, letting him go to his night's work (or taking him along), without having him arrested.",
              "to": "hobb-talks"
            },
            {
              "id": "hobb-runs",
              "when": "Hobb's nerve has gone and he's bolting for the door (at the word 'arrest', or at the thought of his master).",
              "to": "on-his-feet"
            },
            {
              "id": "mum-safe",
              "on": "attempt",
              "when": "The player tries to get Hobb's mum kept safe tonight, out of the Master's reach, by asking someone here who could give her that to take her in (Kell, for a night in her own room or at the watch house; Dilly, aboard the Dabchick at the foot of the stairs; Nan, who knows every bolt-hole on the stairs), where it could go either way. (Promising it with nothing behind it isn't this, and nor is the player going across the city themselves before the bell.)",
              "check": {
                "reason": "to get someone to take Hobb's mum in tonight",
                "skill": "persuasion",
                "dc": 12,
                "success": "Whoever was asked grumbles and gives way: Kell, for one night in her own room, and it goes in the book ('One night. It's written down.'); or Dilly, aboard the Dabchick under the onions, as long as nobody in a uniform sets foot on her; or Nan, who has a word with a widow on the landing who owes her. Someone will fetch her from the Shambles tonight, before the Master thinks to look. Hobb looks from one of them to the other for a long moment, and his shoulders come down: he believes it. If he hasn't told it yet, it starts now, very quietly: 'I only held the rope.'",
                "failure": "Whoever was asked won't, not like that and not tonight (Kell won't call her room a safe house or keep it from her own notebook; Dilly won't have the watch anywhere near her barge; Nan won't have the gentleman's trouble on her stairs), and Hobb heard the no: he's nearer the door for it. But the need is out in the open now, and the others in the room haven't been asked.",
                "onSuccess": "confession",
                "establishes": {
                  "success": [
                    "Hobb's mum is to be kept safe tonight: someone here has agreed to take her in, out of the Master's reach, and she'll be fetched from the Shambles before he thinks to look.",
                    "Big Hobb has broken and begun to tell the player what he did, the loft first: he held the clerk while his master killed him, and hauled the rope. The rest (his master's name, the Heron) comes as he's asked."
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "mum-taken-in",
              "given": true,
              "when": "Someone here has agreed to take Hobb's mum in tonight, out of the Master's reach (Kell, for a night in her own room; Dilly, aboard the Dabchick; Nan, with the widow on the landing who owes her), and Hobb has heard it. He believes it, and his shoulders come down: if he hasn't told it yet, it starts now, very quietly ('I only held the rope.'), and the rest comes as he's asked.",
              "to": "confession",
              "establishes": [
                "Hobb's mum is to be kept safe tonight: someone here has agreed to take her in, out of the Master's reach, and she'll be fetched from the Shambles before he thinks to look.",
                "Big Hobb has broken and begun to tell the player what he did, the loft first: he held the clerk while his master killed him, and hauled the rope. The rest (his master's name, the Heron) comes as he's asked."
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "bribe-cob",
              "towards": "prouts-page",
              "when": "The player offers coin, or more stew, as the price of a look in Cob's boot (to Cob, or to Nan for him), and nothing more (no appeal to what he's afraid of, no promise that answers it): Cob haggles, boasts and takes what's going, but the boot stays on, and Nan won't sell a look in a child's boot either. Bought attention isn't trust. What's really wrong comes out instead, his way: not out here, not with the big cove looking, and what happens to Cob after? (A meal stood him with nothing asked back is a kindness, not this.)",
              "to": "confession"
            },
            {
              "id": "kind-to-cob",
              "towards": "prouts-page",
              "when": "The player does Cob a kindness with nothing asked back: stands him his dinner or an extra bowl with no strings, or gives it freely after he's eaten. He takes it with bad grace and a boast, and it counts with him: after it, a polite ask for a look in his boot, out of the big cove's sight, gets a yes.",
              "to": "confession",
              "establishes": [
                "Cob has had a kindness from the player with nothing asked back (his dinner or an extra bowl stood him with no strings): it counts with him."
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "trust-cob",
              "essential": "prouts-page",
              "when": "Out of the big cove's sight (in the scullery, or anywhere the fireside can't see), the player asks Cob for a look after giving him real reason to trust them (a kindness with nothing asked back, like his dinner stood him with no strings), or makes him a promise, now or before, that truly answers what he's afraid of (his name kept out of it, the big cove put away where he can't come back for him, the boots his to keep, whatever's in the boot going to the King and not the watch), or he has already told them they can look; or Nan, given a reason plainly good for the boy, tells him to. No dice, however it's put: Cob takes the left boot off and lets them unpick the lining: Prout's page is out.",
              "to": "confession",
              "establishes": [
                "Prout's page is out of the lining of Cob's left boot: razored from the Royal Granary Roll, a dozen King's Road grain wagons marked 'lost to goblins', each countersigned 'J. Sallow, for the Royal Purveyor', with Prout's pencilled river-warehouse weights and, at the foot, 'Not goblins. Who pays the hedge-folk?'"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "coax-cob",
              "on": "attempt",
              "essential": "prouts-page",
              "when": "Out of the big cove's sight (in the scullery, or anywhere the fireside can't see), before Cob has any reason to trust them (no kindness with nothing asked back done him yet tonight, no promise that answers what he's afraid of, no yes from him already), the player asks Cob to show them what crackles in his left boot (taking it off, or letting them unpick the lining), politely and with the boots staying his, or tries to win him round to it by reaching him (an appeal to what he cares about: Mister Prout, the men from the loft, his own skin; or a tale he might swallow), where it could go either way. Paying for a look isn't this. (After a kindness with nothing asked back, for someone he really trusts, for a promise that truly answers what he's afraid of, or once he's said they can look, it needs no dice. Out in the room, under the big cove's eye, he won't, and says so his way: not out here.)",
              "check": {
                "reason": "to get Cob to show you what's in his boot",
                "skill": "persuasion",
                "dc": 13,
                "success": "Cob looks past them at the scullery door, and the fire beyond it, for a long moment. Then he sits on an upturned pot, unlaces the left boot and picks the lining open with a dirty thumbnail, muttering that if this is a trick Cob'll know. Out comes a page, folded small and gone soft at the corners, and he holds it out like it might bite: 'That's Mister Prout's writing. That's why it crackled.' He can't read it; anyone who can sees a dozen grain wagons 'lost to goblins', each countersigned 'J. Sallow, for the Royal Purveyor'. If he heard the posh cove ask for 'the page' that night, it comes together for him now, and he goes white.",
                "failure": "Cob won't, and it costs, whichever fits where and how they tried: in the scullery, he's out through the slop hatch Nan told him never to use and down onto the wet steps under it, and her face says whose fault that is; or he yells for Mrs Q, and Nan comes round the bar to ask what the player wants with her pot-boy's boots; or, out in the room, his yelp turns heads, and in the fireside corner Hobb looks up and sees who's bothering the boy. The boot isn't lost: Cob comes back for his stew, warier, and real trust or Nan's word can still open it.",
                "onSuccess": "confession"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "nan-vouches",
              "on": "attempt",
              "essential": "prouts-page",
              "when": "The player asks Nan to tell Cob to show them what's in his boot (or to vouch for them to the boy), giving her a reason, where it could go either way. Paying her for it isn't this. (A reason plainly good for the boy, his name kept out of it and the big man's sort kept off him, needs no dice.)",
              "check": {
                "reason": "to get Nan to tell Cob to show you his boot",
                "skill": "persuasion",
                "dc": 12,
                "success": "Nan looks at the player for a long moment, then wipes her hands and calls through to the scullery: 'Cob. Here, my duck. Show them your boot.' And because it's Nan, he does, sulking: the left one off, the lining picked open, a folded page held out at arm's length. 'That's Mister Prout's.'",
                "failure": "Nan says the boy's boots are the boy's business, and that's a rule of the house now if it wasn't before. She keeps Cob by her behind the bar the rest of the night, and an eye on the player. The boy himself might still be won, if he's given real reason.",
                "onSuccess": "confession"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "page-shown",
              "essential": "prouts-page",
              "given": true,
              "when": "Prout's page has come out of the lining of Cob's left boot and the player has it in hand or has read it: Cob unpicked it for them or let them (trusting them, for a promise that answered his fear, or on Nan's word), or it came out some other way.",
              "to": "confession",
              "establishes": [
                "Prout's page is out of the lining of Cob's left boot: razored from the Royal Granary Roll, a dozen King's Road grain wagons marked 'lost to goblins', each countersigned 'J. Sallow, for the Royal Purveyor', with Prout's pencilled river-warehouse weights and, at the foot, 'Not goblins. Who pays the hedge-folk?'"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "bell-talked",
              "on": "cue",
              "when": "The player has had Hobb's story a while (at least five exchanges at this point) without deciding what becomes of him: the eleventh bell, and Hobb has to go to work.",
              "to": "hobb-talks"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hobb-talks",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 960,
        "y": -660
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "What Big Hobb knows",
        "description": "## Outcome\n\nBig Hobb has told the player what he knows, or the heart of it: at the least, his part in the loft (he held the clerk's arms while his master killed him, then hauled him up on the rope), and as much of the rest as they asked for (his master's name, the Heron warehouse and how to get in at night). The player is leaving the Rat with it, and it's in Kell's notebook as he said it. Hobb isn't under arrest and hasn't run: he's going to his night's work at the Heron, as their man inside if he agreed to be, or keeping his head down if not.\n\n## Closing\n\nClose on the player leaving the Rat with what they came for: Hobb's face as they go (or his broad back going down the stairs ahead of them at the bell), Nan's look, the river below. Kell closes her notebook on it.",
        "lore": [
          "Places/The Drowned Rat.md",
          "World/Caerwyn now.md",
          "World/Fronts.md"
        ],
        "sourceId": "hobb-talks",
        "sourceFile": "scenes/drowned-rat.ts",
        "sourceExit": {
          "id": "hobb-talks",
          "kind": "progress",
          "title": "What Big Hobb knows",
          "outcome": "Big Hobb has told the player what he knows, or the heart of it: at the least, his part in the loft (he held the clerk's arms while his master killed him, then hauled him up on the rope), and as much of the rest as they asked for (his master's name, the Heron warehouse and how to get in at night). The player is leaving the Rat with it, and it's in Kell's notebook as he said it. Hobb isn't under arrest and hasn't run: he's going to his night's work at the Heron, as their man inside if he agreed to be, or keeping his head down if not.",
          "closing": "Close on the player leaving the Rat with what they came for: Hobb's face as they go (or his broad back going down the stairs ahead of them at the bell), Nan's look, the river below. Kell closes her notebook on it.",
          "next": "wharf-night",
          "script": "(world, outcome) => {\n        const hobb = world.character(\"hobb\");\n        const named = has(outcome.established, NAMED);\n        hobb.moveTo(\"heron-warehouse\");\n        hobb.remember(named ? \"He told the King's investigator what happened in the tally loft, and who his master is.\" : \"He told the King's investigator what he did in the tally loft. He didn't say his master's name.\");\n        if (has(outcome.established, INSIDE)) world.promise({ by: \"hobb\", to: \"player\", what: \"Open the Heron's river door to the player tonight and keep the gang off them.\" });\n        keepToken(world, outcome);\n        kellRecords(world, outcome, { always: true });\n        world.setFlag(\"hobb_identified\", true);\n        heronLead(world);\n        world.quest(\"purveyors-man\").advance(\"hobb_talked\", `Big Hobb Mallory says ${named ? \"Master Sallow\" : \"his master\"} killed Prout in the tally loft while Hobb held his arms, and had Hobb hoist him; the stolen grain goes through the Heron warehouse.`);\n        world.journal(`${named ? \"Big Hobb talked: he held Prout in the loft while Master Sallow killed him.\" : \"Big Hobb owned to the loft: he held Prout while his master killed him, and hauled the rope.\"} The grain goes through the Heron warehouse, and tonight a barge is loading there.`);\n        mumKeptSafe(world, outcome);\n        keepPage(world, outcome);\n      }"
        },
        "exitKind": "progress",
        "next": "wharf-night",
        "file": "Scenes/The wharves after dark.kmscene",
        "entry": "downtime",
        "destinationKind": "scene",
        "scriptSource": "(world, outcome) => {\n        const hobb = world.character(\"hobb\");\n        const named = has(outcome.established, NAMED);\n        hobb.moveTo(\"heron-warehouse\");\n        hobb.remember(named ? \"He told the King's investigator what happened in the tally loft, and who his master is.\" : \"He told the King's investigator what he did in the tally loft. He didn't say his master's name.\");\n        if (has(outcome.established, INSIDE)) world.promise({ by: \"hobb\", to: \"player\", what: \"Open the Heron's river door to the player tonight and keep the gang off them.\" });\n        keepToken(world, outcome);\n        kellRecords(world, outcome, { always: true });\n        world.setFlag(\"hobb_identified\", true);\n        heronLead(world);\n        world.quest(\"purveyors-man\").advance(\"hobb_talked\", `Big Hobb Mallory says ${named ? \"Master Sallow\" : \"his master\"} killed Prout in the tally loft while Hobb held his arms, and had Hobb hoist him; the stolen grain goes through the Heron warehouse.`);\n        world.journal(`${named ? \"Big Hobb talked: he held Prout in the loft while Master Sallow killed him.\" : \"Big Hobb owned to the loft: he held Prout while his master killed him, and hauled the rope.\"} The grain goes through the Heron warehouse, and tonight a barge is loading there.`);\n        mumKeptSafe(world, outcome);\n        keepPage(world, outcome);\n      }"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "taken-in",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 960,
        "y": -330
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "Taken in",
        "description": "## Outcome\n\nSergeant Kell has arrested Big Hobb, on evidence she accepts, and is taking him up the river stairs to the watch-house cells. Whatever he told the player before he was taken, they have, and whatever he owned to is in Kell's notebook as he said it; he won't be at the Heron tonight.\n\n## Closing\n\nClose on the arrest done by the book outside Nan's door: Kell's proper words, Hobb's great shoulders going down, the Rat silent behind them, the river below. Kell will see him locked up and come on to wherever the investigator is going next.",
        "lore": [
          "Places/The Drowned Rat.md",
          "World/Caerwyn now.md",
          "World/Fronts.md"
        ],
        "sourceId": "taken-in",
        "sourceFile": "scenes/drowned-rat.ts",
        "sourceExit": {
          "id": "taken-in",
          "kind": "progress",
          "title": "Taken in",
          "outcome": "Sergeant Kell has arrested Big Hobb, on evidence she accepts, and is taking him up the river stairs to the watch-house cells. Whatever he told the player before he was taken, they have, and whatever he owned to is in Kell's notebook as he said it; he won't be at the Heron tonight.",
          "closing": "Close on the arrest done by the book outside Nan's door: Kell's proper words, Hobb's great shoulders going down, the Rat silent behind them, the river below. Kell will see him locked up and come on to wherever the investigator is going next.",
          "next": "wharf-night",
          "script": "(world, outcome) => {\n        const hobb = world.character(\"hobb\");\n        hobb.moveTo(\"watch-house\");\n        hobb.remember(\"Sergeant Kell arrested him outside the Drowned Rat for the clerk's death, with the King's investigator there.\");\n        world.character(\"kell\").remember(\"She arrested Big Hobb Mallory for Prout's murder outside the Drowned Rat and took him to the watch-house cells.\");\n        kellRecords(world, outcome);\n        keepToken(world, outcome);\n        world.setFlag(\"hobb_identified\", true);\n        if (knowsHeron(outcome)) heronLead(world);\n        world.quest(\"purveyors-man\").advance(\"hobb_arrested\", \"Big Hobb Mallory, the big man with the bandaged hand, is in the watch-house cells.\");\n        world.journal(\"Kell took Big Hobb in. He's in the watch-house cells tonight.\");\n        mumKeptSafe(world, outcome);\n        keepPage(world, outcome);\n      }"
        },
        "exitKind": "progress",
        "next": "wharf-night",
        "file": "Scenes/The wharves after dark.kmscene",
        "entry": "downtime",
        "destinationKind": "scene",
        "scriptSource": "(world, outcome) => {\n        const hobb = world.character(\"hobb\");\n        hobb.moveTo(\"watch-house\");\n        hobb.remember(\"Sergeant Kell arrested him outside the Drowned Rat for the clerk's death, with the King's investigator there.\");\n        world.character(\"kell\").remember(\"She arrested Big Hobb Mallory for Prout's murder outside the Drowned Rat and took him to the watch-house cells.\");\n        kellRecords(world, outcome);\n        keepToken(world, outcome);\n        world.setFlag(\"hobb_identified\", true);\n        if (knowsHeron(outcome)) heronLead(world);\n        world.quest(\"purveyors-man\").advance(\"hobb_arrested\", \"Big Hobb Mallory, the big man with the bandaged hand, is in the watch-house cells.\");\n        world.journal(\"Kell took Big Hobb in. He's in the watch-house cells tonight.\");\n        mumKeptSafe(world, outcome);\n        keepPage(world, outcome);\n      }"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hobb-fled",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 960,
        "y": 0
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "Hobb runs",
        "description": "## Outcome\n\nBig Hobb has run from the Rat and got away into the dark. Frightened out of his wits, he's gone where his feet always take him: to his master, to warn him that the King's investigator and a watch sergeant are asking about the loft. Whatever he told the player before he ran, they have, and whatever he owned to is in Kell's notebook as he said it.\n\n## Closing\n\nClose on the empty doorway, the wet stairs and the dark; the Rat's silence, and Nan's look, which says whose fault that was.",
        "lore": [
          "Places/The Drowned Rat.md",
          "World/Caerwyn now.md",
          "World/Fronts.md"
        ],
        "sourceId": "hobb-fled",
        "sourceFile": "scenes/drowned-rat.ts",
        "sourceExit": {
          "id": "hobb-fled",
          "kind": "other",
          "title": "Hobb runs",
          "outcome": "Big Hobb has run from the Rat and got away into the dark. Frightened out of his wits, he's gone where his feet always take him: to his master, to warn him that the King's investigator and a watch sergeant are asking about the loft. Whatever he told the player before he ran, they have, and whatever he owned to is in Kell's notebook as he said it.",
          "closing": "Close on the empty doorway, the wet stairs and the dark; the Rat's silence, and Nan's look, which says whose fault that was.",
          "next": "wharf-night",
          "script": "(world, outcome) => {\n        const hobb = world.character(\"hobb\");\n        hobb.leaveScene(\"ran off up the river stairs into the city, to warn his master\");\n        hobb.setAttitude(\"unfriendly\", \"The King's investigator frightened him out of the Drowned Rat.\");\n        hobb.remember(\"He ran from the Drowned Rat to warn Master Sallow that the King's investigator and a watch sergeant are asking about the loft.\");\n        world.setFlag(\"hobb_identified\", true);\n        world.setFlag(\"sallow_warned\", true);\n        if (knowsHeron(outcome)) heronLead(world);\n        kellRecords(world, outcome);\n        world.journal(\"Big Hobb ran from the Drowned Rat, and he'll have gone straight to his master.\");\n        mumKeptSafe(world, outcome);\n        keepPage(world, outcome);\n      }"
        },
        "exitKind": "other",
        "next": "wharf-night",
        "file": "Scenes/The wharves after dark.kmscene",
        "entry": "downtime",
        "destinationKind": "scene",
        "scriptSource": "(world, outcome) => {\n        const hobb = world.character(\"hobb\");\n        hobb.leaveScene(\"ran off up the river stairs into the city, to warn his master\");\n        hobb.setAttitude(\"unfriendly\", \"The King's investigator frightened him out of the Drowned Rat.\");\n        hobb.remember(\"He ran from the Drowned Rat to warn Master Sallow that the King's investigator and a watch sergeant are asking about the loft.\");\n        world.setFlag(\"hobb_identified\", true);\n        world.setFlag(\"sallow_warned\", true);\n        if (knowsHeron(outcome)) heronLead(world);\n        kellRecords(world, outcome);\n        world.journal(\"Big Hobb ran from the Drowned Rat, and he'll have gone straight to his master.\");\n        mumKeptSafe(world, outcome);\n        keepPage(world, outcome);\n      }"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "thrown-out",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 960,
        "y": 330
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "Manners",
        "description": "## Outcome\n\nNan Quill has thrown the player (and anyone who sided with them) out of the Drowned Rat with Manners, and barred them. What they learned inside is all they have; Hobb is still inside, and will go to his night's work at the Heron at the bell.\n\n## Closing\n\nClose on the wet river stairs outside the barred door, the din starting up again inside, and whatever the player is nursing (an ear, a shin, their pride). If Kell is out there with them, she says something dry about doors.",
        "lore": [
          "Places/The Drowned Rat.md",
          "World/Caerwyn now.md",
          "World/Fronts.md"
        ],
        "sourceId": "thrown-out",
        "sourceFile": "scenes/drowned-rat.ts",
        "sourceExit": {
          "id": "thrown-out",
          "kind": "other",
          "title": "Manners",
          "outcome": "Nan Quill has thrown the player (and anyone who sided with them) out of the Drowned Rat with Manners, and barred them. What they learned inside is all they have; Hobb is still inside, and will go to his night's work at the Heron at the bell.",
          "closing": "Close on the wet river stairs outside the barred door, the din starting up again inside, and whatever the player is nursing (an ear, a shin, their pride). If Kell is out there with them, she says something dry about doors.",
          "next": "wharf-night",
          "script": "(world, outcome) => {\n        const nan = world.character(\"nan-quill\");\n        nan.setAttitude(\"unfriendly\", \"Broke the house rules in the Drowned Rat.\");\n        nan.remember(\"She threw the King's investigator out of the Rat with Manners, and barred them.\");\n        world.character(\"hobb\").moveTo(\"heron-warehouse\");\n        if (has(outcome.established, IDENTIFIED) || has(outcome.established, TALKED)) world.setFlag(\"hobb_identified\", true);\n        if (knowsHeron(outcome)) heronLead(world);\n        kellRecords(world, outcome);\n        world.journal(\"Thrown out of the Drowned Rat by Nan Quill and her cudgel, Manners.\");\n        mumKeptSafe(world, outcome);\n        keepPage(world, outcome);\n      }"
        },
        "exitKind": "other",
        "next": "wharf-night",
        "file": "Scenes/The wharves after dark.kmscene",
        "entry": "downtime",
        "destinationKind": "scene",
        "scriptSource": "(world, outcome) => {\n        const nan = world.character(\"nan-quill\");\n        nan.setAttitude(\"unfriendly\", \"Broke the house rules in the Drowned Rat.\");\n        nan.remember(\"She threw the King's investigator out of the Rat with Manners, and barred them.\");\n        world.character(\"hobb\").moveTo(\"heron-warehouse\");\n        if (has(outcome.established, IDENTIFIED) || has(outcome.established, TALKED)) world.setFlag(\"hobb_identified\", true);\n        if (knowsHeron(outcome)) heronLead(world);\n        kellRecords(world, outcome);\n        world.journal(\"Thrown out of the Drowned Rat by Nan Quill and her cudgel, Manners.\");\n        mumKeptSafe(world, outcome);\n        keepPage(world, outcome);\n      }"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "gone-to-work",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 960,
        "y": 660
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "Hobb goes to work",
        "description": "## Outcome\n\nHobb has gone off to his night's work at the Heron without telling the player what he knows, and the player has left the Rat too: after him to follow, or before him to wait in the dark.\n\n## Closing\n\nClose on Hobb's broad back going down the river stairs towards the wharves, his lantern swinging, and the player at the top of the steps in the dark.",
        "lore": [
          "Places/The Drowned Rat.md",
          "World/Caerwyn now.md",
          "World/Fronts.md"
        ],
        "sourceId": "gone-to-work",
        "sourceFile": "scenes/drowned-rat.ts",
        "sourceExit": {
          "id": "gone-to-work",
          "kind": "leave",
          "title": "Hobb goes to work",
          "outcome": "Hobb has gone off to his night's work at the Heron without telling the player what he knows, and the player has left the Rat too: after him to follow, or before him to wait in the dark.",
          "closing": "Close on Hobb's broad back going down the river stairs towards the wharves, his lantern swinging, and the player at the top of the steps in the dark.",
          "next": "wharf-night",
          "script": "(world, outcome) => {\n        world.character(\"hobb\").moveTo(\"heron-warehouse\");\n        if (has(outcome.established, IDENTIFIED)) world.setFlag(\"hobb_identified\", true);\n        if (knowsHeron(outcome)) heronLead(world);\n        kellRecords(world, outcome);\n        world.journal(\"Big Hobb went off to his night's work at the bell without telling us what he knows.\");\n        mumKeptSafe(world, outcome);\n        keepPage(world, outcome);\n      }"
        },
        "exitKind": "leave",
        "next": "wharf-night",
        "file": "Scenes/The wharves after dark.kmscene",
        "entry": "downtime",
        "destinationKind": "scene",
        "scriptSource": "(world, outcome) => {\n        world.character(\"hobb\").moveTo(\"heron-warehouse\");\n        if (has(outcome.established, IDENTIFIED)) world.setFlag(\"hobb_identified\", true);\n        if (knowsHeron(outcome)) heronLead(world);\n        kellRecords(world, outcome);\n        world.journal(\"Big Hobb went off to his night's work at the bell without telling us what he knows.\");\n        mumKeptSafe(world, outcome);\n        keepPage(world, outcome);\n      }"
      }
    }
