      "id": "route:[\"beat\",\"the-rat\",\"win-hobb\",2,\"success\"]",
      "source": "the-rat",
      "target": "confession",
      "type": "smoothstep",
      "label": "Win hobb · success",
      "data": {
        "condition": "The player tries to talk Hobb into telling what he did and who he does it for, with an appeal, an argument, a bargain or a promise of protection, while he's still holding out and it could go either way. (Just asking isn't this; a kindness or a trade that truly answers his fear needs no dice.)",
        "phase": "attempt",
        "skill": "persuasion",
        "dc": 14,
        "scope": "beat",
        "branch": "success",
        "outcomeText": "Something gives. Hobb looks at his wrapped hand for a long moment and says, very quietly, 'I only held the rope.' The loft comes out first, haltingly; the rest will come as he's asked.",
        "sourceRoute": {
          "id": "win-hobb",
          "on": "attempt",
          "when": "The player tries to talk Hobb into telling what he did and who he does it for, with an appeal, an argument, a bargain or a promise of protection, while he's still holding out and it could go either way. (Just asking isn't this; a kindness or a trade that truly answers his fear needs no dice.)",
          "check": {
            "reason": "to get Big Hobb to tell you what he did",
            "skill": "persuasion",
            "dc": 14,
            "success": "Something gives. Hobb looks at his wrapped hand for a long moment and says, very quietly, 'I only held the rope.' The loft comes out first, haltingly; the rest will come as he's asked.",
            "failure": "Hobb shakes his head and drinks, and his eyes go to the door: not here, not yet. He heard it, though, and he's closer to leaving.",
            "onSuccess": "confession",
            "establishes": {
              "success": [
                "Big Hobb has broken and begun to tell the player what he did, the loft first: he held the clerk while his master killed him, and hauled the rope. The rest (his master's name, the Heron) comes as he's asked."
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "establishes": [
          "Big Hobb has broken and begun to tell the player what he did, the loft first: he held the clerk while his master killed him, and hauled the rope. The rest (his master's name, the Heron) comes as he's asked."
